    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d237">

                <pb facs="0379" n="303" xml:id="pg303"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">862.20/732: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Atherton</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-03-18T19:00:00+00:00">March 18, 1935—7
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received March 18—3:05 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>117. Report from Berlin states that Germans gave immediate favorable answer to
                    British Ambassador when he presented note contained in my 116, March 18, 5
                    p.m.</p>
                <p>Foreign Office has just informed press that Simon and Eden will leave for Berlin
                    Sunday as planned.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Atherton</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
